{"event_type":"review","id":"d981d9c2add88fc89a099f2e0cff1bba8de691e84f7fb54268a6375048427e6a","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T08:50:36Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/edf99e623bc5704bdd363d6aab326dd99205236499d942731057f532e23be17f","sha256":"edf99e623bc5704bdd363d6aab326dd99205236499d942731057f532e23be17f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d21c1bba9b676dfc4eaa13ceec072271e5d883a1bb2a84e1c93dec3af37935e0","sha256":"d21c1bba9b676dfc4eaa13ceec072271e5d883a1bb2a84e1c93dec3af37935e0"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c9e0fa1889a0817e61d84a9c282729a4bedeabd4a31ac45e6e52bd748516d1b2","sha256":"c9e0fa1889a0817e61d84a9c282729a4bedeabd4a31ac45e6e52bd748516d1b2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3a5fe66d8b1275119acffe746fb863c641ce8eae7c487b586ba41da85cf8236c","sha256":"3a5fe66d8b1275119acffe746fb863c641ce8eae7c487b586ba41da85cf8236c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d6867e1d3b36bd02d2bdf34ecae5fe82aec38ae6914d44273e7bb9c576b49a0e","sha256":"d6867e1d3b36bd02d2bdf34ecae5fe82aec38ae6914d44273e7bb9c576b49a0e"}],"attempt_id":"bee6ffaaf62c50e7ab2dbea2a2a1feddb7af78bddeae9ec472f94bedb504ba31:0:1","base":"1c627a86c206a76b94df7266fc1fe2ede1afb31b","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a23c02ee18b025cc87f311e3dde693095a2b9932","body":"**Make the response-cache write non-fatal after the mutation is sent (`src/ops/review/submit.ts:147-159`).**\n\nThe comment on Line 147 says the immutable request stays the recovery authority if the cache update fails. The code does not follow that comment. `readFile`, `writeFile` or `rename` can throw here, for example on a full disk or a removed record file. The error then reaches the `catch` on Line 173. `reviewOp` maps it to `indeterminate`.\n\nThe queue has already admitted the submission at this point. The caller loses the admission `response`. The `waitMs` observation is skipped. The caller must retry with the same `requestId` to recover.\n\nWrap the cache update in its own `try/catch` and continue with `response`. Keep the `requestId` reconcile hint only for real failures.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        const record = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, 'utf8')) as Record<string, unknown>;\n-        const updated = join(dir, requestId + '.' + randomUUID() + '.tmp');\n-        await writeFile(\n-          updated,\n-          JSON.stringify({\n-            ...record,\n-            response,\n-            ...('identity' in response ? { identity: response.identity } : {}),\n-          }),\n-          { mode: 0o600 },\n-        );\n-        await rename(updated, path);\n+        try {\n+          const record = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, 'utf8')) as Record<string, unknown>;\n+          const updated = join(dir, requestId + '.' + randomUUID() + '.tmp');\n+          await writeFile(\n+            updated,\n+            JSON.stringify({\n+              ...record,\n+              response,\n+              ...('identity' in response ? { identity: response.identity } : {}),\n+            }),\n+            { mode: 0o600 },\n+          );\n+          await rename(updated, path);\n+        } catch {\n+          // Cache-only update. The saved wire still lets a retry reconcile this request.\n+        }\n```\n</details>","id":"d17f835c7b0f55ace9e449ea15412c66f815e7a2488ed0f911af84f91936fa9e","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/submit.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the response-cache write non-fatal after the mutation is sent (`src/ops/review/submit.ts:147-159`)."}],"head":"10ce89ec8559a921a0c01f017fc99807718b93ab","head_tree":"1393f525755319d0614b0af7f33278d124294c49","input_scope":[{"blob":"fb4583a892516b18084d